{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196800-why-do-lupus-form-claws-do-bashing-damage","id":1196800,"title":"Why do Lupus-form claws do bashing damage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-18T08:21:03-07:00","id":1196800,"title":"Why do Lupus-form claws do bashing damage?","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> I've seen a small contradiction. Now, I'm not a storyteller myself at our game, so I do not get to choose the rules.<br /> <br /> I was wondering what you guys think about Lupus-form claws doing bashing damage.<br /> Under General Combat Maneuvers -&gt; Claw, it says that Glabro or Lupus forms do bashing damage, while under the Lupus form explanation says the following:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In game terms, a Lupus-form Garou can bite for aggravated<br /> damage, but inflicts only lethal damage with his<br /> claws. Lupus-breed werewolves inflict only lethal damage<br /> with either attack in this shape </div> </div> </div>That's a tiny contradiction - what do you guys think? Typo or just a simple mistake? Or perhaps it was meant to be bashing in the first place?<br /> <br /> Best regards,<br /> TataCavalier<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T08:43:28-07:00","id":1196810,"title":"","content":"It's simply a mistake. Assume lethal damage to be true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T08:59:24-07:00","id":1196816,"title":"","content":"Natural wolf claws aren't really that sharp, so it doesn't really bug me if they do bashing.<br /> <br /> Bashing also means that the lupus-form can be used for fights without it getting deadly fast. Since bites are agg (or lethal for Lupus characters), the lupus form doing lethal claw attacks means it has extremely limited options for trying to subdue something in a non-lethal fashion (basically you can tackle a lot).<br /> <br /> But really, it's not that big of a deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T02:22:19-07:00","id":1197092,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying it's that big of a deal, I was just confused due to the contradiction.<br /> <br /> Anywho, thank you both for the replies!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T03:05:15-07:00","id":1197100,"title":"","content":"I think the intent was Wolf fangs do Lethal, and their claws do bashing because wolves don't claw things to death like cats, they bite things. But they have sizable enough paws where you can get clawed in a scuffle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T17:06:25-07:00","id":1197787,"title":"","content":"Lupus claws are like rooster beaks, they do bashing at 3 successes and under on the attack roll, more than that is lethal, well wolf claws are not big but if they get you a good swipe they can make minor bleeding, experience with both roosters and dogs here. Thats highly coinsidental though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 03-20-2018, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T17:39:30-07:00","id":1197802,"title":"","content":"I decided to say wolf claws do lethal damage in my game, I even considered letting glabro do lethal with claws to.<br /> <br /> Eventually I let the players decided, difficulty 6 if you want to do bashing, difficulty 8 if you want to do agg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T19:16:17-07:00","id":1197833,"title":"","content":"I like Glabro to have claws, but I don't want to deter punches by giving them full on claws. So semi claws works for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}